    "dependencies": [
      "zlib (reuse LMX::zlib)",
      "MPI C (parallel profile)",
      "POSIX/Windows threads",
      "host math/dynamic loader"
    ],
    "selected_profile": "Static C99 core + full HL (H5LT H5DO H5DS H5IM H5PT H5TB H5LD), MPI parallel, pthread atomic emulation, zlib, C99 complex, map/deprecated API; float16 and C++/Fortran/Java bindings disabled",
    "availability_notes": [
      "Parallel profile defines H5_HAVE_PARALLEL; LMX_HDF5_PARALLEL=OFF builds same C code collection without MPI I/O entry points.",
      "HDF5_ENABLE_THREADSAFE=OFF because upstream rejects thread-safe plus HL without unsupported override; LMX must serialize library calls across actors. Pthread primitives are compiled; that is not concurrent-call safety.",
      "H5M map API included; actual map operations depend on a supporting VOL connector, native connector is not claimed to implement maps.",
      "Optional HDFS/ROS3/direct/mirror/subfiling driver sources are preserved; external VOL/filter packages are not bundled. Driver availability follows generated H5pubconf.h; provider-backed APIs additionally require an installed provider.",
      "HDF5_ENABLE_PLUGIN_SUPPORT=OFF means no external hdf5_plugins package; H5PL loader APIs are still compiled.",
      "MPI runtime test limited to one rank; no claim of multi-rank communication in restricted host."
    ],
